{"name":"Silver Strand Beach","hex":"#cacdca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"},{"term":"strand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore or beach of the sea or ocean.","The shore or beach of a lake or river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground; to beach.","To run aground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver Strand Beach","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Strand Beach is an unincorporated beach neighborhood in Ventura County, California, United States. Lying between the mouth of Channel Islands Harbor on the north and the ocean entrance to the Port of Hueneme on the south, the eastern side of the beach community lies along the boundary of the Naval Construction Battalion Center Port Hueneme. The harbors and the Naval base almost completely surround Silver Strand, keeping the area relatively separate from the city of Oxnard and making it accessible by only one main road, Victoria Avenue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Silver_Strand_State_Beach_San_Diego%2C_California_Aerial_Photography.jpg/330px-Silver_Strand_State_Beach_San_Diego%2C_California_Aerial_Photography.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Strand_Beach","wikidata":"Q7516406"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver","wikidata":"Q1090"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)","wikidata":"Q317802"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg/500px-Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg/1280px-Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg/500px-Silver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver Strand Beach, January 2015","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilver-Strand-Beach-California.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Mural_Wall_SSB.jpg/330px-Mural_Wall_SSB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Mural_Wall_SSB.jpg/330px-Mural_Wall_SSB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mural Wall at The Ship parking lot, Silverstrand Beach.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMural_Wall_SSB.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/1280px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A